    <statement><p>Which is a parametric equation for the curve <m>y = 8-6x</m>?</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(t,8+t\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(t,6+t\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(8t,6t\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(t,8-6t\right)</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>P = (0, 8)</m> with slope <m>m = - 6</m>.  Using the parametric representation of a line, we obtain <m>c(t) = \left(t,8-6t\right)</m>.


</solution>
